  "limitations": [
    "No new performance, throughput, multi-GPU scaling or block-width calibration claim",
    "Eight MI300X SPX/NPS1 and eight H200 MIG-disabled devices; no new partition/MIG certification",
    "Coordinator evidence uses isolated localhost mTLS on each host; no public deployment",
    "Legacy CPU -I and -m behavior remains unchanged"
  ],
  "findings": [
    "Nonunit stride coverage uses one-based candidate indices with an immutable affine mapping",
    "Version-2 bindings contain original scalar bounds and stride, preserving version-1 job identities for stride one",
    "Direct arithmetic rejects overflow; stepped caches use modular SG powers without modular candidate enumeration",
    "A seventh worker capability gates strided work before mutation or cached replies",
    "Canonical API fixture errors and corrected reruns are preserved",
    "Malformed submitted mappings return HTTP 400; persisted mapping corruption retains state-unavailable semantics"
  ],
  "evidence_policy": "Phased source and binary-bound acceptance. Search binaries precede storage/worker integration. The API-boundary fix has focused release, sanitizer, HIP and CUDA checks. A final explicit empty optional initializer removes compiler warnings without changing version-1 behavior, with storage/coordinator reruns. Earlier fixture failures remain in the raw logs beside successful corrections. The archive excludes credentials and journal databases."
}
